cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this code, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "klebers-conjecture: Lean verification of Kleber's conjecture and complementary products of symmetric functions"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of R. Hodges, H. Yin, "Kleber's conjecture and
  complementary products of symmetric functions": over every commutative ring,
  the products of Schur functions indexed by the unordered complementary pairs
  in a rectangle are linearly independent (Kleber's conjecture, Theorem 1.1),
  and so are the products indexed by the splittings of a partition
  (Theorem 1.2); the same holds for products of Koike-Terada universal
  characters over every field (Corollary 1.3) and for products of monomial
  symmetric functions over fields of characteristic zero and over the integers
  (Theorem 1.4), together with every other statement of the paper.
  Accompanying libraries develop partitions as Young diagrams, the lattice of
  set partitions, and the ring of symmetric functions over any commutative ring.
authors:
